{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789213906,"nonce":"tkSTdu/RGWCucCN3oi8i+5XvmGA=","title":"Conservative native stack scanning for the Immix collector","message":"Replace precise native-stack roots with a conservative scan when the Immix strategy is active. Roots become read-only; nothing needs writing back.\n\n- At collection entry spill callee-saved registers into a stack buffer (#[inline(never)] asm: aarch64 x19-x28, x86_64 rbx/rbp/r12-r15), take probe = min(current sp, \u0026buf), scan [probe, stack_top) word by word. Stack top from pthread_get_stackaddr_np / pthread_getattr_np, registered once per thread that runs a VM.\n- Candidate word: raw address inside the heap, or a NaN-boxed object (bits \u0026 TAG_OBJ == TAG_OBJ) whose 48-bit payload is inside the heap. Resolve through containing_allocation so interior pointers (ObjUpvalue.location = obj+32) retain the owner. Everything else is ignored.\n- krio fibers: every suspended fiber's [saved_sp, stack_top) is scanned (krio spills callee-saved registers at the switch). If a collection fires inside a fiber, scan the fiber's live window and the host stack from caller_sp. Replaces Pass 3 of scan_native_stack_roots and the krio_jit_roots swap.\n- Precise roots that are not on the stack stay: api_stack, handles, core class fields, fiber frames, module vars, AOT root regions, callbacks.\n\n- Cranelift user stack maps -\u003e SafepointMetadata -\u003e scan_native_stack_roots Pass 1/2, code_ranges, __sps/__roots AOT blobs, wlift_aot_register_code_range, JIT_FRAME_STACK and the naked wren_call_N fp capture, force-frame-pointers, AOT_GC_ENABLED gating (collection can then fire from any allocation in any tier).\n- push_jit_root / jit_root_at / with_rooted_args / root_saved_jit_context (~60 sites), plugin push_root/reload_root become no-ops (symbols kept, ABI version unchanged).\n- conservative_fp_chain_forward_fixup and the spill-slot writeback loop.\n\nA JIT frame that holds only a pointer into a malloc'd payload (ObjInstance.fields, ObjList.elements, ObjTypedArray.data) after the owner pointer died keeps nothing alive. Keep declare_value_needs_stack_map on as a liveness/spill mechanism for now (it forces Values to stack slots across calls, which is exactly what the scanner reads), and move payload buffers into the Immix heap in the performance workstream so interior pointers suffice.\n\nOut of scope here: wasm has no scannable native stack. Tracked separately (shadow stack issue).","files":null}]}